Ms. Padgett,<br />
<br />
The staff's deficiency letter arising from examination 2012-0122 of Rosslyn=
 Padgett Investment Counsel (SEC File No. 801-65310) is attached. There are=
 three items, all of which concern the firm's wrap fee program.<br />
<br />
Item 1 is disclosure. Appendix 1 to Part 2A states that the wrap fee covers=
 "all transaction costs," which is not accurate for the fixed income sleeve=
, where the firm directs trades to dealers on a net basis and the markup is=
 borne by the client in addition to the wrap fee.<br />
<br />
Item 2 is the firm's annual determination that the wrap program remains sui=
table for each participating client. The staff found no documentation of th=
at determination for 2010 or 2011 for 63 of the 210 wrap accounts sampled.<=
br />
<br />
Item 3 is the reasonableness review of the aggregate wrap fee against the c=
ost of the component services, which the firm's own procedures require annu=
ally and which was last performed in 2008.<br />
<br />
A written response is due within 30 days.<br />
<br />
Rosalind Achterberg<br />
Branch Chief, Investment Adviser / Investment Company Examinations<br />
Philadelphia Regional Office